{{- /*
     Where a model release's images come from.

     The hang-watcher, CART and CART's two sidecars: ours, so they sit under
     `registry`, the same way autoconfig's and bodylog's images do. Applies in
     every mode -- a model release is not a special case, and none of this
     depends on whether the cluster is offline.

     The chart's own defaults point at a private registry deliberately (its values explain
     why: the CART subchart defaults to a public registry, which a production
     cluster with no outbound network cannot reach). Naming them here rather
     than inheriting those keeps a bundle built from the public environment
     from having to carry private-registry spellings of images it already holds, and
     keeps that host out of the ones an air-gapped node has to mirror.

     This file is mounted AFTER the entry's own `values:`, because the engine
     rule below transforms what the entry declared -- run first, it would be
     overwritten by the very value it read. The four sidecars are therefore not
     overridable per entry either, which is the same deal every other release in
     this repo gets: its images come from `registry`.

     Tags are left to the chart: an empty tag means its appVersion, which its
     CI rewrites on every release, and pinning one here would freeze it.
     cart.ha and cart.reload are the exception, because that chart writes them
     as a single "repository:tag" string -- replacing the repository replaces
     the tag too, so it has to be supplied. They are autoconfig's sidecars and
     take its version.
*/}}
{{- /*
     The ENGINE. The site declares it once, at its real address, in its own
     `models:` entry -- sglang and vllm are upstream projects and what runs here
     is a build of the site's own, so the address is not ours to invent. What IS
     ours is the same rule every other image follows under `rewrite`: the host
     comes off and `registry` goes on, exactly where offline_load.sh put it.
     Under `upstream` and `mirror` the address is used as declared, because
     those two modes do not rewrite anything.

     This is read back out of .Values.models rather than passed in, because a
     values file cannot see the loop variable -- but it can see the environment,
     and .Release.Name says which entry is ours.
*/}}
{{- $declared := "" }}
{{- range (dig "models" (list) .Values) }}
{{-   if eq .name $.Release.Name }}{{ $declared = dig "values" "image" "repository" "" . }}{{ end }}
{{- end }}
{{- if and $declared (eq (.Values.registryMode | default "upstream") "rewrite") }}
{{- /* host off, path kept -- `a.b/c/d` -> `c/d`, a bare `c/d` unchanged */}}
{{-   $head := splitList "/" $declared | first }}
{{-   $path := ternary (trimPrefix (printf "%s/" $head) $declared) $declared (or (contains "." $head) (contains ":" $head)) }}
image:
  repository: {{ .Values.registry }}/{{ $path }}
{{- end }}
hangWatcher:
  image:
    repository: {{ .Values.registry }}/hang-watcher
cart:
  image:
    repository: {{ .Values.registry }}/cache_aware_router
  ha:
    image: {{ printf "%s/autoconfig-hagate:%s" .Values.registry .Values.versions.autoconfig | quote }}
  reload:
    image: {{ printf "%s/autoconfig-reload:%s" .Values.registry .Values.versions.autoconfig | quote }}
